"""Canonical world country/territory registry — single source of truth for the
"one entry per country" diaspora/origins coverage goal.

Generated from ISO 3166-1 (via pycountry) on 2026-07-23. 249 entries: all UN member
states + officially-coded dependent territories/islands (Réunion, Martinique, Guam,
Puerto Rico, French Polynesia, etc. all have their own ISO codes and appear here).

Each entry: {"iso2", "iso3", "name" (official ISO), "display_name" (common/short name")
used across the site UI), "continent", "ancestral_link"}.

"ancestral_link" points every single country to the "out-of-africa" STORY entry
(seed_data.py) — the one universal, well-sourced fact that all non-African human
populations descend from the same ~70,000-year-old African dispersal. This is
deliberately a single shared reference rather than 249 copies of the same paragraph.

Where a country ALSO has a genuinely distinct, separately sourced deep-ancestry
finding (e.g. the "southern coastal route" relic populations, documented Melanesian
admixture, the Greenland cold-adaptation gene study), that lives as its own entry in
WORLD_DIASPORA_COMMUNITIES (data/world_diaspora.py) — see the ids listed in
ANCESTRAL_DEEP_DIVE_IDS below for the current list of countries with this extra,
country-specific layer beyond the shared universal reference.
"""

